1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:11,000
LiveSync is a tool to connect Marvelous Designer with a virtual editor.

2
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:20,000
With this feature, Marvelous Designer can connect to virtual editors and import and export files seamlessly.

3
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:28,000
To download the necessary files required to install the virtual engine, please click on the main menu to help Marvelous Designer LiveSync.

4
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:37,000
A web page will pop up, you can learn more information and download the plugin on this page.

5
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:44,000
Scroll down this page, you can learn more information, click on Get LiveSync, you can start downloading the plugin.

6
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:49,000
In addition, please check the manual on the Connect page to understand how to install and use this plugin.

7
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:55,000
Please download the Substance 3D virtual engine plugin first, so that you can use the Substance material on Marvelous Designer clothing.

8
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:58,000
Otherwise, the clothing will use the default material.

9
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:06,000
Unzip the downloaded zip file and install LiveSync to virtual engine 5.3.

10
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:11,000
Please put the Cloud LiveSync file in the plugin folder of your virtual engine.

11
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:18,000
The path is as follows, Epic Games, UE5.3, Engine, Plugins, Marketplace.

12
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:25,000
In this folder, you can see that there is also a Substance 3D plugin folder.

13
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:27,000
Open it.

14
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:32,000
Open the Unreal project.

15
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:42,000
Please make sure that the Cloud LiveSync and Substance 3D plugin are already available in the plugin settings.

16
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:51,000
You can go to Edit, Project Settings, then go to the Windows project, and set the default RHI value to DirectX11.

17
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:56,000
Please note that setting DirectX12 may cause the virtual engine 5.3 to crash accidentally through the drive program.

18
00:01:56,000 --> 00:02:03,000
Please note that setting DirectX12 may cause the virtual engine 5.3 to crash accidentally through the drive program.

19
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:12,000
Search for transparency, open and enable the experimental option to remove the local transparency.

20
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:15,000
Then restart the virtual editor.

21
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:20,000
To use the unified material option, please confirm that the UV picture is correctly arranged in the non-folded part.

22
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:23,000
To use the unified material option, please confirm that the UV picture is correctly arranged in the non-folded part.

23
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:26,199
Go to the window of the virtual machine and click on the CloudMD LiveSync Editor.

24
00:02:28,800 --> 00:02:34,000
Click on the update button to import the costume and virtual model into the CloudMD LiveSync Editor.

25
00:02:36,599 --> 00:02:41,099
Please make sure that there is no active simulation or recording animation in Marvelous Designer.

26
00:02:41,500 --> 00:02:46,300
And please switch to the simulation mode or UV editor mode, then click on the update button.

27
00:02:46,300 --> 00:02:54,800
In the virtual machine, the created color changer will match the fabric used in Marvelous Designer.

28
00:02:55,700 --> 00:03:01,500
The Unified Material option is very useful when applying it to the costume or when there are multiple secondary documents.

29
00:03:06,500 --> 00:03:11,800
Please note that you can select the costume or virtual model from the left of the editor by clicking on the object list on the left.

30
00:03:11,800 --> 00:03:13,900
Then press the delete button to delete.

31
00:03:16,300 --> 00:03:29,300
When you are sure that the assets in the LiveSync Editor have been uploaded to the virtual machine content browser, please select the assets you need from the list on the left.

32
